    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The rider's claim that this trip was driven further than the booked route is measured on the platform's GPS trace, and the ruling is NO_ACTION: the charge of SGD 20.64 stands, no refund is due and no compensation is payable.\n\nWhy there is no deviation. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH tests to pass: the excess must be greater than 20% of the optimal distance AND greater than 0.8 km. The governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 14.39 km on EV-GPS-02841, which the clause says prevails over the rounded trip_record copy. Against the booked optimal of 12.0 km (EV-TRIP-02841) the excess is 2.39 km. That is 19.92% of optimal, below the 20% gate, although it clears the 0.8 km absolute test. The trip record's rounded 14.4 km would give exactly 20.0%, which is still not 'greater than 20%', and the trace figure governs in any event. Because one establishment test fails, POL-RD-01 says no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. The rider conceded this rather than stretching it, and the driver's reading reaches the same place.\n\nBilling integrity. EV-FARE-02841 (weight 1.0) reconciles: 3.80 base fare + 10.80 distance (14.4 km x 0.75) + 5.24 time (18.7 min x 0.28) + 0.80 platform fee = 20.64. There are no ERP or toll lines (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.0, derived erp_lines.total 0.00), no airport surcharge and no phantom gantry, so POL-RD-09(4) gives nothing to refund and no billing-integrity referral arises.\n\nRider's fare arithmetic. The rider correctly set out that had a deviation been established, POL-RD-02 would recompute the fare at 18.08 SGD (20.64 - 18.08 = 2.56, rounded up to 2.60 payable, 12.4% of the charge, above the 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share). That route is not reached, because no deviation is established, so no amount is awarded.\n\nDriver's de minimis argument, rejected on its merits. The driver's claim that the refund 'quantum' is 0.05 SGD and